A **region** is a piece of the page with its own rendering and waking rules. It is ogygia's only primitive: every marked import — an island, a server island, a lake, a held region — compiles to the same `<Region>` envelope. They are not four features. They are four settings of one thing.

::: tip Why one primitive
One envelope means one hydration story, one signing story, one props story, and one mental model. When you understand a region, you understand all of them — the rest of this section is just the settings.
:::

## The two dials

A region is configured by two independent dials, set as import attributes:

| Dial | Question it answers | Values |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `render` | Where does the HTML come from, and when? | inline in the page's SSR pass (default) · `'deferred'` — fetched from a signed endpoint per request |
| `wake` | Does this ship client JS, and when does it run? | none (default — HTML only) · `'load'` · `'idle'` · `'visible'` · `'interaction'` · a media query · `'none'` (explicitly frozen) |

Every combination is legal, and each named kind is just a point in that grid:

## The kinds

| Kind | Mark | What it is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Client island](/docs/regions/client-islands) | `with { wake: 'visible' }` | SSRs inline, hydrates on a schedule. The interactive one. |
| [Server island](/docs/regions/server-islands) | `with { render: 'deferred' }` | HTML rendered per fetch from a signed endpoint — fresh on every request, streams into a static shell. Optionally wakes after arrival. |
| [Lake](/docs/regions/lakes) | `with { wake: 'none' }` | Frozen server HTML. Ships zero JS, survives SPA swaps untouched. |
| [Held region](/docs/regions/held-regions) | `region(Comp, props)` | A region as a **value** — minted in a load or remote function, passed over the wire, placed with `<Region of={value} />`. |

Anything unmarked is not a region at all — it's plain server HTML compiled into the page, the default and the cheapest thing on the site.

## What every region guarantees

Whatever the dials say, the envelope's contract is the same:

- **SSR first.** A region renders real HTML on the server. JS, if any, attaches to that HTML — it never replaces it. Disable JS and the markup is still there.
- **One hydration.** A region hydrates exactly once, adopting its server DOM in place — no discard-and-recreate, no flash. Nested regions degrade into their parent's single hydration.
- **Signed capabilities.** Anything a region fetches later — a deferred hole, an SWR remount — goes through an endpoint minted with an HMAC capability at SSR time. The client holds a ticket, not an open door.
- **Props cross by value.** Captured host values cross the boundary via devalue — plain data, `Map`/`Set`/`Date`, and your registered [transportables](/docs/data-state/state-context). Functions and promises don't; state that must live, lives inside the region.

## Shared mechanics

Two pages in this section apply to every kind rather than any one of them:

- [Timing & nesting](/docs/regions/timing-nesting) — the full `wake` schedule reference, `visible` margins, and what happens when regions contain regions.
- [Client islands](/docs/regions/client-islands) — mark an import with `wake` and it ships JS on a schedule; the marked import is a real component binding you can pass around, render dynamically, or put in an `{#each}`.

From here, read the kind you need — or start with [client islands](/docs/regions/client-islands), the one most pages reach for first.

